    "scope": "Inspect six colour/shape classes, two tone classes, held-out classification and temperature calibration.",
    "limitations": [
      "Small generated tasks and fixed splits do not establish natural-image perception, speech recognition, general instruction following or broad multimodal reasoning.",
      "Greedy generation and intervention scores are measured separately; successful loading on generated input is not accuracy evidence.",
      "Temperature is chosen on validation only; the tiny synthetic test estimates do not guarantee calibration improvement or stable bin estimates.",
      "The original-template test has only 6 vision and 14 tone examples: 6/6 and 11/14 are correct. Both validation-selected temperatures are 0.5; positive scaling leaves class argmax unchanged and does not make a generated answer a calibrated statement of truth.",
      "Audio test confidence metrics worsen after the validation-selected scaling: NLL 0.2776→0.3465, Brier 0.2021→0.2534 and ECE 0.1319→0.1415. Validation fitting is not evidence of test calibration improvement.",
      "vision.pt/audio.pt store raw classifier+encoder weights; chosen T=0.5 is not baked into either file. Temperature is a post-hoc evaluation parameter in evaluation.json/model-card metrics, not calibrated confidence that a generated answer is true."
